From fc7d94b64bac15a72b5881dd2a712af409fa0722 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TuNV <tunguyenvanbn94@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 15:24:55 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] [icwmp mtk] Brace the CWMP_LOG branches: the macro carries
 its own ";"

  ../sdk/mtk/icwmp_mtk.c:179:4: error: expected '}' before 'else'

inc/log.h:45 defines the logger with a trailing semicolon:

  #define CWMP_LOG(SEV,MESSAGE,args...) puts_log(SEV,MESSAGE,##args);

so an unbraced branch expands to "if (x) puts_log(...); ;" -- the if statement
ends at the first semicolon and the null statement that follows leaves the
else with no if to bind to.  Upstream icwmp never writes CWMP_LOG as the body
of an if that has an else, so the hazard had not shown up before.

Braced both branches of the secret/non-secret log in
icwmp_mtk_sync_easycwmp_to_cwmp(), and the single-branch CWMP_LOG in
icwmp_platform_init() as well -- that one compiles either way today, but it is
the same construct and the next statement added under it would break silently.

The errors after line 179 (conflicting types for uci_free_context, and the
three "expected identifier" lines) are the parser falling out to file scope;
there is one defect here, not five.

check-c-sanity.py gains a layer for this: a macro whose definition ends in ";"
used as the unbraced body of an if that is followed by else.  Brace counting
cannot see it -- it counts before the preprocessor runs.

NOT BUILD-TESTED on this host: no compiler here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 public/apps/icwmp/icwmp/sdk/mtk/icwmp_mtk.c | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/public/apps/icwmp/icwmp/sdk/mtk/icwmp_mtk.c b/public/apps/icwmp/icwmp/sdk/mtk/icwmp_mtk.c
index d051778..715968a 100644
--- a/public/apps/icwmp/icwmp/sdk/mtk/icwmp_mtk.c
+++ b/public/apps/icwmp/icwmp/sdk/mtk/icwmp_mtk.c
@@ -174,10 +174,14 @@ int icwmp_mtk_sync_easycwmp_to_cwmp(void)
 			continue;
 		if (uci_set_str(c, m->cwmp, v) == 0) {
 			changed = 1;
-			if (is_secret(m->cwmp))
+			/* Braces are load-bearing: inc/log.h defines CWMP_LOG with a
+			 * trailing ";", so an unbraced branch leaves a null statement
+			 * between the if and the else ("expected '}' before 'else'"). */
+			if (is_secret(m->cwmp)) {
 				CWMP_LOG(INFO, "sync easycwmp->cwmp %s (masked)", m->cwmp);
-			else
+			} else {
 				CWMP_LOG(INFO, "sync easycwmp->cwmp %s=%s", m->cwmp, v);
+			}
 		}
 	}
 	if (changed)
@@ -232,8 +236,9 @@ int icwmp_platform_init(void)
 	struct stat st;
 
 	/* backup session file and boot flag live here (bin/Makefile.am CWMP_BKP_FILE) */
-	if (stat(ICWMP_MTK_STATE_DIR, &st) != 0 && mkdir(ICWMP_MTK_STATE_DIR, 0755) != 0)
+	if (stat(ICWMP_MTK_STATE_DIR, &st) != 0 && mkdir(ICWMP_MTK_STATE_DIR, 0755) != 0) {
 		CWMP_LOG(ERROR, "cannot create %s: %s", ICWMP_MTK_STATE_DIR, strerror(errno));
+	}
 	icwmp_mtk_sync_easycwmp_to_cwmp();
 	return 0;
 }
